# Findings Trivy should stop reporting, each with the reason it is safe here.
# Anything in this file has been read and judged rather than waved through, and
# a finding with an available fix does not belong in it. Prefer upgrading.

# CVE-2024-23342 — python-ecdsa, the Minerva timing attack.
#
# No fixed version exists. The maintainers have said the pure-Python library
# cannot be made constant-time and will not carry a fix, so there is nothing to
# upgrade to.
#
# It reaches the image as a hard dependency of python-jose and is never
# exercised. The attack is a timing side channel on ECDSA signing, and this
# platform signs nothing with ECDSA. Access tokens use RS256
# (`jwt_algorithm` in apps/api/app/core/config.py) and the SSO state token
# uses HS256 (apps/api/app/routers/sso.py). Neither touches the ecdsa code
# path.
#
# Revisit if `jwt_algorithm` is ever set to ES256, ES384 or ES512, at which
# point this entry must come out and the dependency has to go.
CVE-2024-23342
